-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 3: EFFECTS OF THE CONTRACT (ss 16 to 26).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Section 22 is "[Not applicable]" in this text: nothing to encode (coverage row s 22).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

-- Helper (Part 3), not a section: an event recorded as a MAYBE DATE has occurred by the date asked about.
GIVEN event IS A MAYBE DATE
      asked IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST happened THEN happened AT MOST asked

§ `Part 3 -- Effects of the contract`

§§ `Transfer of property as between seller and buyer (ss 16 to 20B)`

-- s 16.  Unascertained goods: no property is transferred until the goods are ascertained (subject to s 20A).
-- src:571 | 16. Subject to section 20A, where there is a contract for the sale of
-- src:572 | unascertained goods, no property in the goods is transferred to the
-- src:573 | buyer unless and until the goods are ascertained.
@ref s 16 (src:571-573)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of unascertained goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 20A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 20A applies`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 20A" -- s 20A gives the buyer an undivided share in the bulk.
            NOTHING
        IF `the contract is for the sale of unascertained goods` AND (NOT `the goods are ascertained`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no property in the goods is transferred to the buyer unless and until the goods are ascertained"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "unless and until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): once the goods are ascertained the section says nothing about when the property passes (ss 17 and 18 do), and it speaks only of "a contract for the sale of unascertained goods".
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer`: the BAR as its own yes/no, "can no property yet be transferred?"
-- Ruling (d) of 2026-11-05 ("until" bars, fork F12) applied to the same words: "no property in the goods is transferred to the buyer unless and until the goods are ascertained". Not named by the ruling's list of three sites; assumed, not ruled.
-- JUST TRUE while the bar is in force (unascertained goods, not yet ascertained); JUST FALSE once they are ascertained, and JUST FALSE where the rule does not reach the contract (no bar).
-- Where section 20A applies the answer is NOTHING, as in the function above: the section is "Subject to section 20A", whose own rule gives the buyer an undivided share in the bulk.
-- src:571 | 16. Subject to section 20A, where there is a contract for the sale of
-- src:572 | unascertained goods, no property in the goods is transferred to the
-- src:573 | buyer unless and until the goods are ascertained.
@ref s 16 bar (src:571-573)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of unascertained goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 20A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16 property in unascertained goods cannot yet be transferred` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `section 20A applies`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 20A" -- s 20A gives the buyer an undivided share in the bulk, and the section does not say whether anything is barred then.
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the contract is for the sale of unascertained goods`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar applies "where there is a contract for the sale of unascertained goods"; otherwise there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the goods are ascertained`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no property in the goods is transferred to the buyer unless and until the goods are ascertained" -- the bar lasts "until" then, so from then on it is not in force. This says nothing about whether property is transferred; that is the value of `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer`, NOTHING from then on. -- (d) applied to the same words: assumed, not ruled
            JUST FALSE

-- s 17(1).  Specific or ascertained goods: the property passes when the parties intend.
-- src:580 | 17.—(1) Where there is a contract for the sale of specific or
-- src:581 | ascertained goods, the property in them is transferred to the buyer at
-- src:582 | such time as the parties to the contract intend it to be transferred.
@ref s 17(1) (src:580-582)
GIVEN `the goods are specific or ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time at which the parties intend the property to be transferred` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 17(1) the time at which the property in the goods is transferred to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the goods are specific or ascertained`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific or ascertained goods". The yes/no twin `s 17(1) the rule that the property passes when the parties intend applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): when the parties intend it is a fact about the parties (s 17(2) says how it is found); a known intended time is passed through, an unknown one is NOTHING.
            `the time at which the parties intend the property to be transferred`

-- Twin of `s 17(1) the time at which the property in the goods is transferred to the buyer`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:580 | 17.—(1) Where there is a contract for the sale of specific or
-- src:581 | ascertained goods, the property in them is transferred to the buyer at
-- src:582 | such time as the parties to the contract intend it to be transferred.
@ref s 17(1) applies (src:580-582)
GIVEN `the goods are specific or ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17(1) the rule that the property passes when the parties intend applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are specific or ascertained`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific or ascertained goods, the property in them is transferred to the buyer at such time as the parties to the contract intend" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 17(2).  How the intention is found.
DECLARE `Source of evidence of the parties' intention` IS ONE OF
    `the terms of the contract`
    `the conduct of the parties`
    `the circumstances of the case`
    `something else`

-- src:584 | (2) For the purpose of ascertaining the intention of the parties,
-- src:585 | regard shall be had to the terms of the contract, the conduct of the
-- src:586 | parties and the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 17(2) (src:584-586)
GIVEN `the source of evidence` IS A `Source of evidence of the parties' intention`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17(2) regard shall be had to this source in ascertaining the intention of the parties` IS
    CONSIDER `the source of evidence`
    WHEN `the terms of the contract` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the conduct of the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the circumstances of the case` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three sources and does not say that no other may be considered.
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- s 18, chapeau.
-- src:590 | 18. Unless a different intention appears, the following are rules for
-- src:591 | ascertaining the intention of the parties as to the time at which the
-- src:592 | property in the goods is to pass to the buyer:
@ref s 18 (src:590-592)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18 the following are rules for ascertaining the intention of the parties as to when the property passes` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a different intention appears, the following are rules for ascertaining the intention of the parties"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "Unless" is read as the text's no when a different intention appears.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 18(a) Rule 1.
-- src:594 | (a) Rule 1.—Where there is an unconditional contract for the
-- src:595 | sale of specific goods in a deliverable state, the property in
-- src:596 | the goods passes to the buyer when the contract is made,
-- src:597 | and it is immaterial whether the time of payment or the
-- src:598 | time of delivery, or both, be postponed.
@ref s 18(a) Rule 1 (src:594-598)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is an unconditional contract for the sale of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are in a deliverable state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the contract was made` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF `the contract is an unconditional contract for the sale of specific goods` AND `the goods are in a deliverable state` AND (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the contract was made`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 1 applies "Where there is an unconditional contract for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state" and says the property passes "when the contract is made"; for another contract, or before that date, it has not passed under this rule. (the third condition reads "when the contract is made" as the date from which the rule runs: fork F10) -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(b) Rule 2.
-- src:600 | (b) Rule 2.—Where there is a contract for the sale of specific
-- src:601 | goods and the seller is bound to do something to the goods
-- src:602 | for the purpose of putting them into a deliverable state, the
-- src:603 | property does not pass until the thing is done and the buyer
-- src:604 | has notice that it has been done.
@ref s 18(b) Rule 2 (src:600-604)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is bound to do something to the goods to put them into a deliverable state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the thing was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the contract is for the sale of specific goods` AND `the seller is bound to do something to the goods to put them into a deliverable state`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 2 applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods and the seller is bound to do something to the goods for the purpose of putting them into a deliverable state". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the thing was done` `the date asked about` AND `helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` `the date asked about`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property does not pass until the thing is done and the buyer has notice that it has been done"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Rule 2 says only when the property does not pass; once the thing is done and the buyer has notice it does not say that the property passes.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer`: the BAR as its own yes/no, "can the property not yet pass?"
-- Ruled 2026-11-05 ("until" bars, fork F12): encode the bar and never claim that the property has passed.
-- JUST TRUE while the bar is in force (the rule applies and the thing is not yet done, or the buyer has not yet had notice, by the date asked about);
-- JUST FALSE once both have happened by that date, and JUST FALSE where the rule does not apply (no bar).
-- The value of the function above is left as it was: JUST FALSE before the event, NOTHING from it.
-- src:600 | (b) Rule 2.—Where there is a contract for the sale of specific
-- src:601 | goods and the seller is bound to do something to the goods
-- src:602 | for the purpose of putting them into a deliverable state, the
-- src:603 | property does not pass until the thing is done and the buyer
-- src:604 | has notice that it has been done.
@ref s 18(b) Rule 2 bar (src:600-604)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is bound to do something to the goods to put them into a deliverable state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the thing was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a different intention appears" -- the rule is displaced, so there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (the "unless" rule of 2026-10-29)
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the contract is for the sale of specific goods` AND `the seller is bound to do something to the goods to put them into a deliverable state`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 2 applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods and the seller is bound to do something to the goods for the purpose of putting them into a deliverable state"; otherwise there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the thing was done` `the date asked about` AND `helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` `the date asked about`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property does not pass until the thing is done and the buyer has notice that it has been done" -- the bar lasts "until" then, so from then on it is not in force. This says nothing about whether the property has passed; that is the value of `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer`, NOTHING from the event on. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (d): an "until" bar is its own yes/no function
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(c) Rule 3.
-- src:606 | (c) Rule 3.—Where there is a contract for the sale of specific
-- src:607 | goods in a deliverable state but the seller is bound to weigh,
-- src:608 | measure, test, or do some other act or thing with reference
-- src:609 | to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price, the
-- src:610 | property does not pass until the act or thing is done and the
-- src:611 | buyer has notice that it has been done.
@ref s 18(c) Rule 3 (src:606-611)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the act or thing was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the contract is for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state` AND `the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 3 applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state but the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test, or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the act or thing was done` `the date asked about` AND `helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` `the date asked about`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property does not pass until the act or thing is done and the buyer has notice that it has been done"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Rule 3 says only when the property does not pass.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer`: the BAR as its own yes/no, "can the property not yet pass?"
-- Ruled 2026-11-05 ("until" bars, fork F12): encode the bar and never claim that the property has passed.
-- JUST TRUE while the bar is in force (the rule applies and the act or thing is not yet done, or the buyer has not yet had notice, by the date asked about);
-- JUST FALSE once both have happened by that date, and JUST FALSE where the rule does not apply (no bar).
-- The value of the function above is left as it was: JUST FALSE before the event, NOTHING from it.
-- src:606 | (c) Rule 3.—Where there is a contract for the sale of specific
-- src:607 | goods in a deliverable state but the seller is bound to weigh,
-- src:608 | measure, test, or do some other act or thing with reference
-- src:609 | to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price, the
-- src:610 | property does not pass until the act or thing is done and the
-- src:611 | buyer has notice that it has been done.
@ref s 18(c) Rule 3 bar (src:606-611)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the act or thing was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a different intention appears" -- the rule is displaced, so there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (the "unless" rule of 2026-10-29)
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`the contract is for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state` AND `the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 3 applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods in a deliverable state but the seller is bound to weigh, measure, test, or do some other act or thing with reference to the goods for the purpose of ascertaining the price"; otherwise there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the act or thing was done` `the date asked about` AND `helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the buyer had notice that it was done` `the date asked about`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property does not pass until the act or thing is done and the buyer has notice that it has been done" -- the bar lasts "until" then, so from then on it is not in force. This says nothing about whether the property has passed; that is the value of `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer`, NOTHING from the event on. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (d): an "until" bar is its own yes/no function
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(d) Rule 4: goods on approval or sale or return.
-- src:613 | (d) Rule 4.—When goods are delivered to the buyer on
-- src:614 | approval or on sale or return or other similar terms, the
-- src:615 | property in the goods passes to the buyer —
-- src:617 | (i) when he signifies his approval or acceptance to the
-- src:618 | seller or does any other act adopting the transaction;
-- src:620 | (ii) if he does not signify his approval or acceptance to
-- src:621 | the seller but retains the goods without giving notice
-- src:626 | of rejection, then, if a time has been fixed for the
-- src:627 | return of the goods, on the expiration of that time,
-- src:628 | and, if no time has been fixed, on the expiration of a
-- src:629 | reasonable time.
@ref s 18(d) Rule 4 (src:613-629)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods were delivered to the buyer on approval or on sale or return or other similar terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the buyer signified approval or acceptance to the seller or did another act adopting the transaction` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the buyer retained the goods without giving notice of rejection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a time has been fixed for the return of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the time fixed for the return of the goods expires` IS A DATE
      `the date a reasonable time for the return of the goods expires` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the goods were delivered to the buyer on approval or on sale or return or other similar terms`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 4 applies "When goods are delivered to the buyer on approval or on sale or return or other similar terms". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `helper (Part 3): the event has occurred by the date asked about` `the date the buyer signified approval or acceptance to the seller or did another act adopting the transaction` `the date asked about`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the buyer retained the goods without giving notice of rejection` AND `a time has been fixed for the return of the goods` AND (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the time fixed for the return of the goods expires`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the buyer retained the goods without giving notice of rejection` AND (NOT `a time has been fixed for the return of the goods`) AND (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date a reasonable time for the return of the goods expires`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 4 says the property passes on approval or adoption, or, if he retains the goods without giving notice of rejection, on the expiration of the fixed time or of a reasonable time; before then, or without that retention, it has not passed under this rule. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (ab): a period the text fixes in its own words, and a "where" condition: outside the period, or with the condition not met, the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(e)(i) Rule 5, first limb.
-- src:631 | (e) Rule 5.—(i) Where there is a contract for the sale of
-- src:632 | unascertained or future goods by description, and goods of
-- src:633 | that description and in a deliverable state are
-- src:634 | unconditionally appropriated to the contract, either by
-- src:635 | the seller with the assent of the buyer or by the buyer with
-- src:636 | the assent of the seller, the property in the goods then
-- src:637 | passes to the buyer; and the assent may be express or
-- src:638 | implied, and may be given either before or after the
-- src:639 | appropriation is made.
@ref s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i) (src:631-639)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of unascertained or future goods by description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `goods of that description and in a deliverable state are unconditionally appropriated to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appropriation is by the seller with the assent of the buyer, or by the buyer with the assent of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the appropriation` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF   `the contract is for the sale of unascertained or future goods by description`
         AND `goods of that description and in a deliverable state are unconditionally appropriated to the contract`
         AND `the appropriation is by the seller with the assent of the buyer, or by the buyer with the assent of the seller`
         AND (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date of the appropriation`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 5(i) says the property passes "then", when goods of that description in a deliverable state are unconditionally appropriated with the other party's assent; the assent "may be given either before or after the appropriation is made". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5, second limb.
-- src:641 | (ii) Where, in pursuance of the contract, the seller delivers the
-- src:642 | goods to the buyer or to a carrier or other bailee or
-- src:643 | custodier (whether named by the buyer or not) for the
-- src:644 | purpose of transmission to the buyer, and does not reserve
-- src:645 | the right of disposal, he is to be taken to have
-- src:646 | unconditionally appropriated the goods to the contract.
@ref s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii) (src:641-646)
GIVEN `the seller delivers the goods in pursuance of the contract to the buyer or to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller reserves the right of disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii): the seller is taken to have unconditionally appropriated the goods to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller delivers the goods in pursuance of the contract to the buyer or to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer` AND (NOT `the seller reserves the right of disposal`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the deeming applies "Where, in pursuance of the contract, the seller delivers the goods to the buyer or to a carrier ... and does not reserve the right of disposal". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5, bulk reduced to the contract quantity.
-- src:648 | (iii) Where there is a contract for the sale of a specified quantity
-- src:649 | of unascertained goods in a deliverable state forming part
-- src:650 | of a bulk which is identified either in the contract or by
-- src:651 | subsequent agreement between the parties and the bulk is
