-- src:657 | to that contract at the time when the bulk is so
-- src:658 | reduced; and
-- src:660 | (B) the property in those goods then passes to that buyer.
@ref s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii) (src:648-660)
GIVEN `a different intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods in a deliverable state forming part of a bulk identified in the contract or by subsequent agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bulk is reduced to (or to less than) that quantity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer under that contract is the only buyer to whom goods are then due out of the bulk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the bulk is reduced` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a different intention appears`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless a different intention appears".
            NOTHING
        IF   `the contract is for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods in a deliverable state forming part of a bulk identified in the contract or by subsequent agreement`
         AND `the bulk is reduced to (or to less than) that quantity`
         AND `the buyer under that contract is the only buyer to whom goods are then due out of the bulk`
         AND (`the date asked about` AT LEAST `the date the bulk is reduced`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 5(iii) applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods ... and the bulk is reduced to (or to less than) that quantity, then, if the buyer under that contract is the only buyer to whom goods are then due out of the bulk". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
