-- s 19(1).  Reservation of the right of disposal.
-- src:673 | 19.—(1) Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods or
-- src:674 | where goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract, the seller
-- src:675 | may, by the terms of the contract or appropriation, reserve the right of
-- src:676 | disposal of the goods until certain conditions are fulfilled; and in such
-- src:677 | a case, notwithstanding the delivery of the goods to the buyer, or to a
-- src:678 | carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to
-- src:679 | the buyer, the property in the goods does not pass to the buyer until
-- src:680 | the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled.
@ref s 19(1) (src:673-680)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of specific goods or the goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has reserved the right of disposal by the terms of the contract or appropriation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is for the sale of specific goods or the goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract` AND `the seller has reserved the right of disposal by the terms of the contract or appropriation` AND (NOT `the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notwithstanding the delivery of the goods to the buyer, or to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer, the property in the goods does not pass to the buyer until the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the no is the text's flat negative "until", read as the text's no for the case before the event, inside the limit it sets; the other reading, (b), takes that limit in its own wording as making the branch NOTHING even before the event.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the property not passing "until the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled"; it does not say that the property passes then.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer`: the BAR as its own yes/no, "can the property not yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved?"
-- Ruling (d) of 2026-11-05 ("until" bars, fork F12) applied to the same words: "the property in the goods does not pass to the buyer until the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled". Not named by the ruling's list of three sites; assumed, not ruled.
-- JUST TRUE while the bar is in force (right of disposal reserved, conditions not yet fulfilled); JUST FALSE once they are fulfilled, and JUST FALSE where nothing was reserved (no bar).
-- src:673 | 19.—(1) Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods or
-- src:674 | where goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract, the seller
-- src:675 | may, by the terms of the contract or appropriation, reserve the right of
-- src:676 | disposal of the goods until certain conditions are fulfilled; and in such
-- src:677 | a case, notwithstanding the delivery of the goods to the buyer, or to a
-- src:678 | carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to
-- src:679 | the buyer, the property in the goods does not pass to the buyer until
-- src:680 | the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled.
@ref s 19(1) bar (src:673-680)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of specific goods or the goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has reserved the right of disposal by the terms of the contract or appropriation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(1) the property cannot yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the contract is for the sale of specific goods or the goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract` AND `the seller has reserved the right of disposal by the terms of the contract or appropriation`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods or where goods are subsequently appropriated to the contract" and the seller has reserved the right of disposal "in such a case"; otherwise there is no bar. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property in the goods does not pass to the buyer until the conditions imposed by the seller are fulfilled" -- the bar lasts "until" then, so from then on it is not in force. This says nothing about whether the property has passed; that is the value of `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer`, NOTHING from then on. -- (d) applied to the same words: assumed, not ruled
            JUST FALSE

-- s 19(2).  Bill of lading to the seller's order: prima facie a reservation.
-- src:682 | (2) Where goods are shipped, and by the bill of lading the goods are
-- src:683 | deliverable to the order of the seller or his agent, the seller is prima
-- src:684 | facie to be taken to reserve the right of disposal.
