    BRANCH
        IF `the seller draws on the buyer for the price and transmits the bill of exchange and bill of lading to the buyer together to secure acceptance or payment of the bill of exchange` AND `the buyer does not honour the bill of exchange`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Where the seller of goods draws on the buyer for the price, and transmits the bill of exchange and bill of lading to the buyer together", "if he does not honour the bill of exchange". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:686 | (3) Where the seller of goods draws on the buyer for the price, and
