-- s 20(1).  Risk goes with property, unless otherwise agreed.
-- src:695 | 20.—(1) Unless otherwise agreed, the goods remain at the seller’s
-- src:696 | risk until the property in them is transferred to the buyer, but when the
-- src:697 | property in them is transferred to the buyer the goods are at the
-- src:698 | buyer’s risk whether delivery has been made or not.
@ref s 20(1) (src:695-698)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property in the goods has been transferred to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Party to the sale`
DECIDE `s 20(1) the party at whose risk the goods are` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is otherwise agreed`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless otherwise agreed"; the subsection does not say whose risk the goods are at under another agreement.
            NOTHING
        IF `the property in the goods has been transferred to the buyer`
        THEN JUST Buyer
        OTHERWISE JUST Seller

-- s 20(2).  Delay through the fault of either party.
-- src:700 | (2) But where delivery has been delayed through the fault of either
-- src:701 | buyer or seller, the goods are at the risk of the party at fault as regards
-- src:702 | any loss which might not have occurred but for such fault.
@ref s 20(2) (src:700-702)
GIVEN `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss might not have occurred but for such fault` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Party to the sale`
DECIDE `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the buyer` AND (NOT `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the seller`) AND `the loss might not have occurred but for such fault`
        THEN JUST Buyer
        IF `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the seller` AND (NOT `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the buyer`) AND `the loss might not have occurred but for such fault`
        THEN JUST Seller
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "where delivery has been delayed through the fault of either buyer or seller" and only "as regards any loss which might not have occurred but for such fault"; where both are at fault it is silent. The yes/no twin `s 20(2) the rule on delay through the fault of a party applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:700 | (2) But where delivery has been delayed through the fault of either
-- src:701 | buyer or seller, the goods are at the risk of the party at fault as regards
-- src:702 | any loss which might not have occurred but for such fault.
@ref s 20(2) applies (src:700-702)
GIVEN `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(2) the rule on delay through the fault of a party applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the buyer` OR `delivery has been delayed through the fault of the seller`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where delivery has been delayed through the fault of either buyer or seller" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if" (the words "as regards any loss which might not have occurred but for such fault" carry no "only" in the text; a loss that would have occurred anyway stays NOTHING in the value function, ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
            JUST FALSE

