        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the duties or liabilities of either seller or buyer as a bailee or custodier of the goods of the other party."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of duties or liabilities as a bailee or custodier.
