-- s 20A(1).  When the section applies.
-- src:709 | 20A.—(1) This section applies to a contract for the sale of a
-- src:710 | specified quantity of unascertained goods if the following conditions
-- src:711 | are met:
-- src:716 | (a) the goods or some of them form part of a bulk which is
-- src:717 | identified either in the contract or by subsequent agreement
-- src:718 | between the parties; and
-- src:720 | (b) the buyer has paid the price for some or all of the goods
-- src:721 | which are the subject of the contract and which form part of
-- src:722 | the bulk.
@ref s 20A(1) (src:709-722)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods or some of them form part of a bulk identified in the contract or by subsequent agreement between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has paid the price for some or all of the goods which are the subject of the contract and which form part of the bulk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20A(1) section 20A applies to the contract` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the contract is for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods`
         AND `the goods or some of them form part of a bulk identified in the contract or by subsequent agreement between the parties`
         AND `the buyer has paid the price for some or all of the goods which are the subject of the contract and which form part of the bulk`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a contract for the sale of a specified quantity of unascertained goods if the following conditions are met"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "if the following conditions are met" is read as the text's no when a condition is not met; the other reading is that "if" gives a sufficient condition only.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 20A(2).  The buyer becomes an owner in common of the bulk; property in an undivided share is transferred.
-- src:724 | (2) Where this section applies, then (unless the parties agree
-- src:725 | otherwise), as soon as the conditions specified in paragraphs (a) and
-- src:726 | (b) of subsection (1) are met or at such later time as the parties may
-- src:727 | agree —
-- src:729 | (a) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to
-- src:730 | the buyer; and
-- src:732 | (b) the buyer becomes an owner in common of the bulk.
@ref s 20A(2) (src:724-732)
GIVEN `section 20A applies to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties agree otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20A(2) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to the buyer and he becomes an owner in common` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `section 20A applies to the contract`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where this section applies". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the parties agree otherwise`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(unless the parties agree otherwise)"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the parties agree otherwise.
