        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:724 | (2) Where this section applies, then (unless the parties agree
-- src:725 | otherwise), as soon as the conditions specified in paragraphs (a) and
-- src:726 | (b) of subsection (1) are met or at such later time as the parties may
-- src:727 | agree —
-- src:729 | (a) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to
-- src:730 | the buyer; and
-- src:732 | (b) the buyer becomes an owner in common of the bulk.
@ref s 20A(2) time (src:724-732)
GIVEN `the date the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met` IS A DATE
      `a later time the parties agree` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 20A(2) the time at which property in the undivided share is transferred` IS
    CONSIDER `a later time the parties agree`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met`
    WHEN JUST agreed THEN
        IF agreed AT LEAST `the date the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met`
        THEN agreed
        ELSE `the date the conditions in subsection (1)(a) and (b) are met`

-- s 20A(3).  The buyer's undivided share: quantity paid for and due out of the bulk, over the quantity in the bulk.
-- src:734 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), for the purposes of this section, the
-- src:735 | undivided share of a buyer in a bulk at any time shall be such share as
-- src:736 | the quantity of goods paid for and due to the buyer out of the bulk
-- src:737 | bears to the quantity of goods in the bulk at that time.
@ref s 20A(3) (src:734-737)
GIVEN `the quantity of goods paid for and due to the buyer out of the bulk` IS A NUMBER
      `the quantity of goods in the bulk at that time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20A(3) the undivided share of the buyer in the bulk` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the quantity of goods in the bulk at that time` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`the quantity of goods paid for and due to the buyer out of the bulk` DIVIDED BY `the quantity of goods in the bulk at that time`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the subsection fixes the share as a proportion of the quantity in the bulk and does not say what the share is of a bulk that holds nothing.
            NOTHING

-- s 20A(4).  If the shares of all buyers would together exceed the whole, each is reduced proportionately.
-- src:739 | (4) Where the aggregate of the undivided shares of buyers in a bulk
-- src:740 | determined under subsection (3) would at any time exceed the whole
-- src:741 | of the bulk at that time, the undivided share in the bulk of each buyer
-- src:742 | shall be reduced proportionately so that the aggregate of the
-- src:743 | undivided shares is equal to the whole bulk.
@ref s 20A(4) (src:739-743)
GIVEN `the undivided share of this buyer determined under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the undivided shares of all buyers determined under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20A(4) the undivided share of this buyer after proportionate reduction` IS
    IF `the aggregate of the undivided shares of all buyers determined under subsection (3)` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `the undivided share of this buyer determined under subsection (3)` DIVIDED BY `the aggregate of the undivided shares of all buyers determined under subsection (3)`
    ELSE `the undivided share of this buyer determined under subsection (3)`

-- s 20A(5).  A delivery out of the bulk is ascribed first to goods paid for.
-- src:745 | (5) Where a buyer has paid the price for only some of the goods due
-- src:746 | to him out of a bulk, any delivery to the buyer out of the bulk shall, for
-- src:747 | the purposes of this section, be ascribed in the first place to the goods
-- src:748 | in respect of which payment has been made.
@ref s 20A(5) (src:745-748)
GIVEN `the quantity of goods the buyer has paid for` IS A NUMBER
      `the quantity delivered to the buyer out of the bulk` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20A(5) the quantity of paid-for goods still to be delivered after the delivery` IS
    IF `the quantity delivered to the buyer out of the bulk` AT LEAST `the quantity of goods the buyer has paid for`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the quantity of goods the buyer has paid for` MINUS `the quantity delivered to the buyer out of the bulk`

-- s 20A(6).  Payment of part of the price is payment for a corresponding part of the goods.
-- src:750 | (6) For the purposes of this section, payment of part of the price for
-- src:751 | any goods shall be treated as payment for a corresponding part of the
-- src:752 | goods.
@ref s 20A(6) (src:750-752)
GIVEN `the quantity of the goods` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the price that has been paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole price for those goods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 20A(6) the quantity of goods treated as paid for` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the whole price for those goods` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`the quantity of the goods` TIMES `the part of the price that has been paid` DIVIDED BY `the whole price for those goods`)
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the subsection treats part payment as payment for "a corresponding part of the goods" and gives no proportion where the price is nil.
            NOTHING

-- s 20B(1).  Deemed consent of a co-owner.
DECLARE `Dealing with the bulk` IS ONE OF
    `a delivery out of the bulk to another owner in common of goods due to him under his contract`
    `a dealing, removal, delivery or disposal of goods in the bulk by another owner in common, within that co-owner's undivided share at the time`
    `some other dealing with the bulk`

-- src:756 | 20B.—(1) A person who has become an owner in common of a
-- src:757 | bulk by virtue of section 20A shall be deemed to have consented to —
-- src:762 | (a) any delivery of goods out of the bulk to any other owner in
-- src:763 | common of the bulk, being goods which are due to him
-- src:764 | under his contract; or
-- src:766 | (b) any dealing with or removal, delivery or disposal of goods
-- src:767 | in the bulk by any other person who is an owner in
-- src:768 | common of the bulk in so far as the goods fall within that
-- src:769 | co-owner’s undivided share in the bulk at the time of the
-- src:770 | dealing, removal, delivery or disposal.
@ref s 20B(1) (src:756-770)
GIVEN `the person became an owner in common of the bulk by virtue of section 20A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealing` IS A `Dealing with the bulk`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20B(1) the owner in common is deemed to have consented to the dealing` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person became an owner in common of the bulk by virtue of section 20A`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who has become an owner in common of a bulk by virtue of section 20A".
            NOTHING
        IF `the dealing` EQUALS `some other dealing with the bulk`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection deems consent to the dealings in paragraphs (a) and (b) and says nothing about others.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 20B(2).
-- src:772 | (2) No cause of action shall accrue to anyone against a person by
-- src:773 | reason of that person having acted in accordance with paragraph (a)
-- src:774 | or (b) of subsection (1) in reliance on any consent deemed to have
-- src:775 | been given under that subsection.
@ref s 20B(2) (src:772-775)
GIVEN `the person acted in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (1) in reliance on a consent deemed to have been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20B(2) a cause of action accrues to anyone against the person who so acted` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person acted in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (1) in reliance on a consent deemed to have been given`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No cause of action shall accrue to anyone against a person by reason of that person having acted in accordance with paragraph (a) or (b) of subsection (1) in reliance on any consent deemed to have been given under that subsection."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a person who so acted in reliance on a deemed consent.
            NOTHING

-- s 20B(3).
DECLARE `Matter that section 20A or 20B does not touch` IS ONE OF
    `an obligation on a buyer out of a bulk to compensate another buyer for a shortfall`
    `a contractual arrangement between buyers for adjustments between themselves`
    `the rights of a buyer under his contract`
    `some other matter under section 20A or 20B`

-- src:777 | (3) Nothing in this section or section 20A shall —
-- src:779 | (a) impose an obligation on a buyer of goods out of a bulk to
-- src:780 | compensate any other buyer of goods out of that bulk for
-- src:781 | any shortfall in the goods received by that other buyer;
-- src:783 | (b) affect any contractual arrangement between buyers of
-- src:784 | goods out of a bulk for adjustments between themselves; or
-- src:786 | (c) affect the rights of any buyer under his contract.
@ref s 20B(3) (src:777-786)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter that section 20A or 20B does not touch`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20B(3) section 20A or 20B imposes or affects the matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or section 20A shall (a) impose an obligation on a buyer of goods out of a bulk to compensate any other buyer of goods out of that bulk for any shortfall in the goods received by that other buyer"
    WHEN `an obligation on a buyer out of a bulk to compensate another buyer for a shortfall` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or section 20A shall ... (b) affect any contractual arrangement between buyers of goods out of a bulk for adjustments between themselves"
    WHEN `a contractual arrangement between buyers for adjustments between themselves` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or section 20A shall ... (c) affect the rights of any buyer under his contract."
    WHEN `the rights of a buyer under his contract` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names three matters and says nothing about any other.
    WHEN `some other matter under section 20A or 20B` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Transfer of title (ss 21 to 26)`

-- s 21(1).  A sale by a non-owner without authority or consent passes no better title than the seller had.
-- src:792 | 21.—(1) Subject to this Act, where goods are sold by a person who
-- src:793 | is not their owner, and who does not sell them under the authority or
-- src:794 | with the consent of the owner, the buyer acquires no better title to the
-- src:795 | goods than the seller had, unless the owner of the goods is by his
-- src:796 | conduct precluded from denying the seller’s authority to sell.
@ref s 21(1) (src:792-796)
GIVEN `the goods are sold by a person who is not their owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he sells under the authority or with the consent of the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner is by his conduct precluded from denying the seller's authority to sell` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21(1) the buyer acquires a better title to the goods than the seller had` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the goods are sold by a person who is not their owner` AND (NOT `he sells under the authority or with the consent of the owner`))
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "where goods are sold by a person who is not their owner, and who does not sell them under the authority or with the consent of the owner".
            NOTHING
        IF `the owner is by his conduct precluded from denying the seller's authority to sell`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the owner of the goods is by his conduct precluded from denying the seller's authority to sell" -- the subsection then says nothing about the buyer's title.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the buyer acquires no better title to the goods than the seller had"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 21(2).
DECLARE `Matter that the Act leaves untouched in s 21(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the provisions of the Factors Act 1889 or an enactment enabling the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if he were their true owner`
    `the validity of a contract of sale under a special common law or statutory power of sale or under the order of a court of competent jurisdiction`
    `some other matter under section 21(2)`

-- src:798 | (2) Nothing in this Act affects —
-- src:800 | (a) the provisions of the Factors Act 1889 or any enactment
-- src:801 | enabling the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as
-- src:802 | if he were their true owner;
-- src:804 | (b) the validity of any contract of sale under any special
-- src:805 | common law or statutory power of sale or under the order
-- src:806 | of a court of competent jurisdiction.
@ref s 21(2) (src:798-806)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Matter that the Act leaves untouched in s 21(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21(2) this Act affects the matter` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects (a) the provisions of the Factors Act 1889 or any enactment enabling the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if he were their true owner"
    WHEN `the provisions of the Factors Act 1889 or an enactment enabling the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if he were their true owner` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Act affects ... (b) the validity of any contract of sale under any special common law or statutory power of sale or under the order of a court of competent jurisdiction."
    WHEN `the validity of a contract of sale under a special common law or statutory power of sale or under the order of a court of competent jurisdiction` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names two matters.
    WHEN `some other matter under section 21(2)` THEN NOTHING

-- s 23.
-- src:815 | 23. When the seller of goods has a voidable title to them, but his
-- src:816 | title has not been avoided at the time of the sale, the buyer acquires a
-- src:817 | good title to the goods, provided he buys them in good faith and
-- src:818 | without notice of the seller’s defect of title.
@ref s 23 (src:815-818)
GIVEN `the seller of the goods has a voidable title to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his title has not been avoided at the time of the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer buys the goods in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer has no notice of the seller's defect of title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the seller of the goods has a voidable title to them` AND `his title has not been avoided at the time of the sale`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "When the seller of goods has a voidable title to them, but his title has not been avoided at the time of the sale". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the buyer buys the goods in good faith` AND `the buyer has no notice of the seller's defect of title`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided he buys them in good faith and without notice of the seller’s defect of title"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "provided" is read as a condition whose failure is the text's no.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 24.
-- src:822 | 24. Where a person having sold goods continues or is in possession
-- src:823 | of the goods, or of the documents of title to the goods, the delivery or
-- src:824 | transfer by that person, or by a mercantile agent acting for him, of the
-- src:825 | goods or documents of title under any sale, pledge, or other
-- src:826 | disposition thereof, to any person receiving the same in good faith
-- src:827 | and without notice of the previous sale, has the same effect as if the
-- src:828 | person making the delivery or transfer were expressly authorised by
-- src:829 | the owner of the goods to make the same.
@ref s 24 (src:822-829)
GIVEN `a person having sold goods continues or is in possession of the goods, or of the documents of title to the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person, or a mercantile agent acting for him, delivers or transfers the goods or documents of title under a sale, pledge or other disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receiving them receives in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receiving them has no notice of the previous sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `a person having sold goods continues or is in possession of the goods, or of the documents of title to the goods`
         AND `that person, or a mercantile agent acting for him, delivers or transfers the goods or documents of title under a sale, pledge or other disposition`
         AND `the person receiving them receives in good faith`
         AND `the person receiving them has no notice of the previous sale`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where a person having sold goods continues or is in possession" and the delivery or transfer is "to any person receiving the same in good faith and without notice of the previous sale". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 25.
-- src:833 | 25. Where a person having bought or agreed to buy goods obtains,
-- src:834 | with the consent of the seller, possession of the goods or the
-- src:835 | documents of title to the goods, the delivery or transfer by that person,
-- src:836 | or by a mercantile agent acting for him, of the goods or documents of
-- src:837 | title, under any sale, pledge, or other disposition thereof, to any
-- src:838 | person receiving the same in good faith and without notice of any lien
-- src:839 | or other right of the original seller in respect of the goods, has the
-- src:840 | same effect as if the person making the delivery or transfer were a
-- src:841 | mercantile agent in possession of the goods or documents of title with
-- src:842 | the consent of the owner.
@ref s 25 (src:833-842)
GIVEN `a person having bought or agreed to buy goods obtains, with the consent of the seller, possession of the goods or the documents of title to the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person, or a mercantile agent acting for him, delivers or transfers the goods or documents of title under a sale, pledge or other disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receiving them receives in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receiving them has no notice of any lien or other right of the original seller in respect of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the person making it were a mercantile agent in possession with the consent of the owner` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `a person having bought or agreed to buy goods obtains, with the consent of the seller, possession of the goods or the documents of title to the goods`
         AND `that person, or a mercantile agent acting for him, delivers or transfers the goods or documents of title under a sale, pledge or other disposition`
         AND `the person receiving them receives in good faith`
         AND `the person receiving them has no notice of any lien or other right of the original seller in respect of the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where a person having bought or agreed to buy goods obtains, with the consent of the seller, possession" and the delivery is "to any person receiving the same in good faith and without notice of any lien or other right of the original seller". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 26.  "Mercantile agent" in ss 24 and 25.
-- src:846 | 26. In sections 24 and 25, “mercantile agent” means a mercantile
-- src:847 | agent having in the customary course of his business as such agent
-- src:848 | authority either —
-- src:850 | (a) to sell goods;
-- src:852 | (b) to consign goods for the purpose of sale;
-- src:857 | (c) to buy goods; or
-- src:859 | (d) to raise money on the security of goods.
@ref s 26 (src:846-859)
GIVEN `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to sell goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to consign goods for the purpose of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to buy goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to raise money on the security of goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26 the person is a mercantile agent for the purposes of ss 24 and 25` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to sell goods`
          OR `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to consign goods for the purpose of sale`
          OR `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to buy goods`
          OR `the agent has in the customary course of his business as such agent authority to raise money on the security of goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In sections 24 and 25, “mercantile agent” means a mercantile agent having in the customary course of his business as such agent authority either (a) to sell goods; (b) to consign goods for the purpose of sale; (c) to buy goods; or (d) to raise money on the security of goods."
            JUST FALSE
